3.  DJANGO / BACKEND PROBLEMS FOUND & FIXED
============================================================

3.1  settings.py — hardening & Vercel compat
--------------------------------------------
PROBLEMS FOUND:
  - No WhiteNoise middleware; static files would 404 on Vercel.
  - SECRET_KEY had a hard-coded dev-only fallback; no env override.
  - DEBUG had no env override.
  - ALLOWED_HOSTS did not auto-include Vercel-provided hosts.
  - No Vercel proxy trust (SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER,
    USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST, CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE, etc.).
  - CORS allowed only http://localhost:5173 / http://127.0.0.1:5173
    and a *single* VERCEL_URL, not *.vercel.app preview hosts.
  - CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS only allowed localhost / single VERCEL_URL.
  - STATICFILES_DIRS not set.
  - FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME did not support env override.
  - AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS existed but no
    AUTH_USER_MODEL override was checked (it IS configured
    correctly to users.User — kept as-is).

FIXES APPLIED (backend/config/settings.py):
  - Added `whitenoise.middleware.WhiteNoiseMiddleware`
    to MIDDLEWARE (directly after SecurityMiddleware).
  - Added SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER = ('HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PROTO', 'https')
  - Added USE_X_FORWARDED_HOST = True
  - Added SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT = False (Vercel terminates SSL for us)
  - Added CSRF_COOKIE_SECURE and SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE:
    True when DJANGO_DEBUG is False, else False.
  - SECRET_KEY now reads from os.environ.get('DJANGO_SECRET_KEY', dev_fallback)
  - DEBUG = (os.environ.get('DJANGO_DEBUG', 'True') == 'True')
  - ALLOWED_HOSTS = [] + env DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS (CSV split)
       + auto VERCEL_URL hostname + .vercel.app wildcard hostnames
  - CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN_REGEXES now includes:
       ^https://.*\.vercel\.app$ , ^https://<vercelurl>$
       localhost/127.0.0.1 on ports 5173 / 4173 / 3000
  - CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS now includes all of:
       localhost/127.0.0.1 variants, http(s)://.vercel.app,
       and the current VERCEL_URL.
  - CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS = True (needed for csrftoken/sessionid)
  - Set STATIC_ROOT = BASE_DIR / 'staticfiles' for WhiteNoise
       + Vercel collectstatic output
  - Added STATICFILES_DIRS = [BASE_DIR / 'static']
  - FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME support via env DJANGO_FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME
  - Added MEDIA_ROOT / MEDIA_URL config (already correct, kept)
  - Installed apps audit: rest_framework, corsheaders,
       products, users, orders — all present.

3.2  urls.py — root URL config
------------------------------
ORIGINAL: included products.urls, users.urls, orders.urls
without /api prefix; admin at /admin/; media via static().

PROBLEM FOUND:
  - Vercel api/index.py routes to WSGI only for paths
    starting with /api /admin /media /static.  The API
    URLs in the original urls.py were at the root level
    (/products/... etc.), so they would have 404'd when
    accessed via /api/products/ on Vercel.

FIX APPLIED:
