============================================================
5.  VERCEL DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION FIXES
============================================================

5.1  api/index.py — CREATED (did not exist)
-------------------------------------------
WSGI entry point used by Vercel serverless Python functions.

Key responsibilities:
  1. Sets sys.path to include both project ROOT and backend/
     folders so `import config.settings` and app imports work.
  2. Sets DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE='config.settings'.
  3. Defines a `_normalize_path()` helper that ensures Django
     sees /api /admin /media /static prefixes correctly even
     when Vercel's routing layer mutates PATH_INFO / SCRIPT_NAME.
     Uses REQUEST_URI as the canonical source when available.
  4. Wraps get_wsgi_application() with error handling that
     catches exceptions during request handling, prints a
     traceback to Vercel runtime logs, and returns a plain
     500 response instead of crashing the serverless worker.
  5. Exposes `app`, `application`, and `handler` callables to
     match the various names different Vercel runtimes look for.

WHY THIS IS NEEDED:
  Vercel runs Python serverless functions via a WSGI shim.
  Without this handler, Django cannot find its settings module
  (since manage.py is not used) and URL routing for
  `/api/...` breaks because Vercel mangles PATH_INFO.

5.2  vercel.json — COMPLETELY REWRITTEN
---------------------------------------
ORIGINAL:
  - Used deprecated multi-"services" block { frontend + backend }
    with custom @vercel/python and @vercel/static-build builders.
  - This format is UNSUPPORTED and causes the Vercel CLI /
    dashboard build to fail.
  - Missing rewrites for frontend routes (SPA catch-all).
  - Missing api/index.py routing.

NEW:
  - Single `buildCommand`: `npm run build` (builds React/Vite)
  - Single `outputDirectory`: `dist` (Vite output)
  - `installCommand`: installs BOTH Python and Node deps by
    running `npm install` + `pip install -r requirements.txt`
    (piped via &&) — Vercel 2025 supports a mixed node+python
    runtime when both package.json and requirements.txt exist
    at the project root.
  - Python version pinned to `3.12` via `functions.python.version`
    (Vercel default, avoids Python 3.14 pin surprises).
  - **Routes (in order)**:
    1. /api/*     -> api/index.py (serverless Python WSGI)
    2. /admin/*   -> api/index.py (Django admin)
    3. /media/*   -> api/index.py (Django serves media via
                      WhiteNoise from backend/media)
    4. /static/*  -> api/index.py (collectstatic output under
                      backend/staticfiles; also WhiteNoise)
    5. /*         -> /index.html (SPA catch-all for React
                      Router history routes)

IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT MEDIA FILES ON VERCEL:
  Vercel serverless functions have EPHEMERAL filesystems.
  Files written to backend/media at runtime (e.g. new product
  uploads via admin panel after deployment) are lost on cold
  start.  Images SHIPPED WITH THE REPO (backend/media/products/*.png)
  will work because they're part of the deployment bundle.
  For persistent media on Vercel, integrate an external
  object store (S3-compatible storage via django-storages +
  Boto3 is the standard pattern).  Documented in Final Report.

