6.2  API service (services/api.js)
----------------------------------
ISSUES:
  - AXIOS_BASE_URL config was `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api` when
    VITE_API_URL is set, but on Vercel we need same-origin /api.
  - No centralised MEDIA_URL helper — frontend constructed
    product image URLs by using the raw image_url field
    returned by the API, which in some cases was a
    Django-relative path (/media/products/foo.png) without
    the origin host; product images would fail to load on
    Vercel if DRF request context was lost (see §3.5).
  - Axios instance was NOT setting withCredentials=true by
    default; CSRF token cookies and session cookies would
    not be sent on cross-origin requests (e.g. local dev with
    5173 <> 8000).

FIXES APPLIED:
  1. Axios instance now defaults `withCredentials: true`.
  2. New export: `API_BASE` helper that picks:
        VITE_API_URL if set & non-empty
        `/api` if same-origin
        http://127.0.0.1:8000/api as last-resort local fallback
  3. New export: `resolveMediaUrl(path)` — if path is a
     complete URL (http/https), return as-is; if path is a
     relative path (e.g. /media/products/x.png), prepend
     API_BASE origin so images load on Vercel even when the
     server returns a relative URL.  Handles empty paths
     (returns null) so components can show a fallback icon.
  4. auth/login/register/csrf helpers continue to work but
     now share the correct origin.
  5. Axios response interceptor now includes 401 / 403
     handling with a graceful logout fallback for expired
     sessions.

