7.2  ProductImage generator (image_utils.py)
--------------------------------------------
backend/products/utils/image_utils.py — CREATED/ENHANCED.
  - generate_product_cover() uses Pillow to draw a high-
    quality cover image sized for the store (800x600).
  - Uses a category-specific color palette so a SHOOTER
    game has a noticeably different background than a
    HORROR game or a CONSOLE product.
  - Uses category-specific EMOJI ICONS so users can tell
    at a glance what kind of product it is (gamepad for
    video games, headphone icon for headsets, gamepad
    face-buttons for controllers, and a console-tower icon
    for consoles):
      action    = ⚔️
      shooter   = 🎯
      sports    = ⚽
      racing    = 🏎️
      strategy  = ♟️
      rpg       = 🗡️
      adventure = 🗺️
      horror    = 👻
      consoles  = 🎮
      accessories (controller) = 🕹️
      accessories (headset)    = 🎧
      default   = 🎮
  - Overlays the product name and (optional) brand/price.
  - Creates the products/ directory automatically if it's
    missing before saving PNG files.
  - generate_category_placeholder(category) exists as a
    helper utility for future empty categories.

HOW TO ENSURE IMAGES ARE CORRECT FOR YOUR CATALOG:
  - If you ever change product names/categories/brands in
    seed_products.py, re-run from the backend/ directory:
        python manage.py seed_products --clear
    This overwrites each generated cover so the VISUAL
    (color + icon + overlaid name) matches the 12 products
    exactly.  No "rename a wrong image to match" — the
    pixel content is regenerated from the product's own
    metadata.
  - The 12 PNGs already present in backend/media/products/
    were generated with an earlier version of image_utils;
    re-running `seed_products --clear` will upgrade them
    to include the new category icons and polished palette.

