8.  DATABASE / MIGRATIONS / DJANGO COMMANDS (TO RUN LOCALLY)
============================================================

Because pip install is restricted in this sandbox, the
end-user MUST run these commands on their own machine from
the backend/ folder AFTER installing Python dependencies
(see §9):

  (1) Install dependencies (preferably inside a venv):
          cd backend
          python -m venv .venv
          .venv\Scripts\activate           # Windows
          pip install -r requirements.txt  # from root dir

  (2) Check for import errors / broken Django config:
          python manage.py check
      (Expected output: "System check identified no issues (0 silenced).")

  (3) Create any fresh migrations (should produce 0 new files
      if existing migrations are up to date with models):
          python manage.py makemigrations

  (4) Apply all migrations to backend/db.sqlite3:
          python manage.py migrate

  (5) Create a superuser (for /admin and admin pages):
          python manage.py createsuperuser
      (Choose username + email + secure password)

  (6) Seed sample products + generated images:
          python manage.py seed_products

  (7) Run the Django dev server on :8000:
          python manage.py runserver

  (8) In a second terminal, run the Vite frontend on :5173:
          cd ..    # (back to project root)
          npm install    # if not yet installed
          npm run dev

  (9) Navigate to:
        http://localhost:5173/            — Storefront
        http://localhost:5173/admin/      — Admin panel
        http://localhost:5173/login       — Login
        http://localhost:5173/register    — Register
        http://localhost:8000/api/products/   — REST API
        http://localhost:8000/admin/      — Django admin

