  DJANGO_DEBUG             "True" for local dev, "False" on
                           Vercel (and any production).
  DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS     Comma-separated list of custom
                           hostnames (e.g. example.com,www.example.com)
                           — VERCEL_URL and *.vercel.app are
                           auto-added by settings.py, so you
                           only need this for custom domains.
  DJANGO_FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME Optional URL prefix (leave EMPTY
                           on Vercel).

  -- Frontend / Vite --
  VITE_API_URL             Only needed for LOCAL dev when
                           Vite (:5173) and Django (:8000)
                           run on different ports.  Set to
                           http://127.0.0.1:8000/api locally.
                           On Vercel do NOT set this —
                           same-origin /api is used automatically.

For Vercel, add the following variables in the Dashboard at
Project Settings → Environment Variables, scoped to
Production + Preview + Development:

  DJANGO_SECRET_KEY          (your generated key; REQUIRED)
  DJANGO_DEBUG               False

If you have a custom domain, also add:
  DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS       example.com,www.example.com

