12. REMAINING ISSUES (EXTERNAL SERVICES / CREDENTIALS)
============================================================

1. EPHEMERAL MEDIA on Vercel serverless — images uploaded
   via Django admin AFTER deployment (new product uploads,
   category images, etc.) are NOT persistent on Vercel
   Serverless Functions' disk.  Solution: switch to an
   external object store (AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, Supabase
   Storage, etc.) via `django-storages` + boto3 package,
   or run Django on a persistent host (Render, Fly.io,
   Railway, EC2, etc.) for mutable state.  The shipped 12
   static product images that are part of the GIT repo
   WILL work on Vercel because they're baked into the
   deployment bundle.

2. Pip install blocked in TRAE sandbox — end-user MUST
   run `pip install -r requirements.txt` locally (see §8)
   before they can execute Django management commands.
   This is a TRAE sandbox restriction, NOT a bug in the
   project, and cannot be fixed from code alone.

3. No real external product imagery source was configured.
   `image_utils.py` generates high-quality placeholder
   covers that visually match each product (category color +
   category icon + product name).  If you need real product
   photography (e.g. real photo of Nova Elite Wireless
   Controller, real box shot of Championship Legends 25),
   you have two options:
   (a) Replace the 12 PNGs in backend/media/products/ with
       real photos you have rights to, keeping the same
       slugified filenames (db + seed command match those
       names).
   (b) Point each Product.image to a remote https URL
       (ImageField accepts URLs if you switch to a custom
       URL-only storage backend, or you could add a second
       `image_external_url` model field for off-site hosting).
   Either way is fully compatible with the current serializer
   (it handles absolute URLs and file-backed images alike).

4. SECRET_KEY: even though settings.py has a dev-only fallback,
   production MUST set DJANGO_SECRET_KEY.  If it's not set,
   Django will still boot with the fallback but this is a
   security risk (same key is published in the git repo).
   ALWAYS override it for any publicly reachable host.

